<TrustPage title={`Affiliate Disclosure — ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="How JayArr Coffee earns from Amazon links, how to tell an exact-product link from an Amazon search, and which links earn nothing. Questions go to jay@jayarr.coffee." kicker="Legal" updated="October 19, 2026">
	<Fragment slot="title">Affiliate <em>disclosure</em></Fragment>

	<h2>How we earn</h2>
	<p>JayArr Coffee is a participant in the <strong>Amazon Services LLC Associates Program</strong>, an affiliate advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon.com.</p>
	<p>Some links on this site are affiliate links. When you buy through one, we may receive a small commission at <strong>no additional cost to you</strong>: the price is the same whether you use our link or go to the retailer directly.</p>

	<h2>Two kinds of Amazon link</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>A specific product.</strong> A link to one product opens that product's own Amazon page. The Grind Calibrator and the Espresso Machine Chooser link exact models this way, as do some articles.</li>
		<li><strong>An Amazon search.</strong> Other links open Amazon's search results for a product's name, not a product page. They say they are searches: the Nespresso pod tool's button reads "Search Amazon for …", and in articles the product name is followed by "(Amazon search)". A search can show other sellers, sizes or models first, so check the listing before you buy.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>Every Amazon link carries our tag (<code>jayarrcoffee-20</code>) and is marked <code>rel="sponsored"</code> in the page source.</p>
	<p>Links to a maker's or shop's own website, such as Nespresso's or an espresso machine maker's own pages, are not affiliate links. We earn nothing from them.</p>

	<h2>Our commitment to honesty</h2>
	<p>Affiliate relationships do not influence our reviews, recommendations or editorial content. We recommend products because we believe they are useful to our readers, not because of the commission we might earn. We will always:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Give honest opinions regardless of affiliate relationships</li>
		<li>Clearly identify when content contains affiliate links</li>
		<li>Only recommend products we would use ourselves</li>
		<li>Prioritize our readers' interests over commission potential</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Where you'll see this disclosure</h2>
	<p>Every page's footer says "As an Amazon Associate, JayArr Coffee earns from qualifying purchases." Most articles with buying links also say so in a short note right after them. <a href="/how-we-make-this/">How we make this</a> explains how we choose what to recommend.</p>

	<h2>FTC compliance</h2>
	<p>This disclosure follows the Federal Trade Commission's guidelines on endorsements and testimonials. For more, see the <a href="https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/resources/ftcs-endorsement-guides-what-people-are-asking" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FTC's Endorsement Guides</a>.</p>

	<h2>Questions</h2>
	<p>Questions about our affiliate links: <a href="mailto:jay@jayarr.coffee">jay@jayarr.coffee</a>.</p>
</TrustPage>
